Grunt wrote:
> Per some of the recent discussion regarding wands of nothing and potions
> of gain ability, I've developed a patch that adds the suggested effect -
> dipping a wand of nothing into a non-cursed potion of gain ability
> causes it to gain an ability, i.e. turn into a wand other than a wand of
> nothing (with the normal item frequencies applied, for the sake of
> balance).  Dipping a wand other than a wand of nothing into a _cursed_
> potion of gain ability will strip it of its ability, turning it into a
> wand of nothing (which can then gain an ability, so one with potions of
> gain ability to spare can try to turn their useless wands into something
> useful).
>
> The act of dipping the wand into such a potion has a (recharge count in
> 7) chance of _not_ incrementing the recharge counter, as with
> polypiling wands.
>
> The patch can be found at:
> http://bilious.homelinux.org/?250
>
> Let me know what you think.

